WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.764 --> 00:04.401 align:center line:81%
Jesus “went about doing good.”

00:05.602 --> 00:08.839 align:center line:79%
We read that simple report
in the book of Acts.

00:09.706 --> 00:14.311 align:center line:81%
What an enormous understatement that is!

00:15.345 --> 00:17.781 align:center line:81%
Jesus surely did go about doing good.

00:18.315 --> 00:22.152 align:center line:79%
He is the very essence
and source of goodness.

00:22.386 --> 00:27.157 align:center line:79%
He devoted His entire
mortal life to doing good.

00:28.258 --> 00:32.596 align:center line:79%
He is merciful and gracious,
longsuffering and abundant,

00:32.596 --> 00:36.199 align:center line:79%
infinite in goodness
and everlasting in mercy.

00:37.167 --> 00:40.804 align:center line:79%
Any attempt at describing
or summarizing His goodness

00:40.804 --> 00:43.874 align:center line:81%
and mercy would be an understatement.

00:44.875 --> 00:48.612 align:center line:79%
Truly, as the Apostle John
tried to express,

00:49.112 --> 00:54.418 align:center line:79%
if we were to attempt to record every
manifestation of the Savior's goodness,

00:54.851 --> 00:59.423 align:center line:79%
“even the world itself could not
contain the books that should be written.”

01:01.325 --> 01:05.529 align:center line:79%
The specific examples we do
have immortalized in scripture

01:05.562 --> 01:07.831 align:center line:81%
of Jesus going about doing good

01:07.931 --> 01:09.600 align:center line:81%
stir deep awe and wonder,

01:10.067 --> 01:14.671 align:center line:79%
especially when we really consider
what it might have been like to be there

01:15.405 --> 01:19.509 align:center line:79%
to witness His miracles,
to receive His teachings,

01:19.977 --> 01:22.479 align:center line:81%
and to experience His healing.

01:23.780 --> 01:26.283 align:center line:81%
He conversed with the social outcasts,

01:26.683 --> 01:29.386 align:center line:81%
He touched the diseased and unclean,

01:29.686 --> 01:31.922 align:center line:81%
He brought comfort to the weary,

01:32.489 --> 01:34.291 align:center line:81%
He taught liberating truth,

01:34.291 --> 01:36.326 align:center line:81%
and He called sinners to repentance.

01:36.860 --> 01:40.564 align:center line:79%
To each leper, blind
man, and adulterous woman;

01:40.931 --> 01:43.700 align:center line:79%
to the lame, the deaf, and the dumb;
to every

01:44.368 --> 01:50.841 align:center line:79%
grieving mother, desperate father,
and mourning widow; to the condemned,

01:50.874 --> 01:55.445 align:center line:79%
the shamed, and the suffering; to the dead
in body and the dead in spirit,

01:55.479 --> 02:00.250 align:center line:81%
what He did was offer a new beginning.

02:01.685 --> 02:05.389 align:center line:81%
Yes, another staggering understatement.

02:06.690 --> 02:11.662 align:center line:79%
Everything He said and did
provided a new beginning for each

02:11.728 --> 02:15.799 align:center line:79%
of those He healed,
blessed, taught, and relieved of sin.

02:16.233 --> 02:22.839 align:center line:79%
He didn’t withdraw from them,
and He certainly won’t withdraw from you.

02:24.708 --> 02:32.282 align:center line:79%
Imagine in this moment, hearing any of
these life-giving words from Him:

02:32.749 --> 02:34.518 align:center line:81%
“Son, thy sins be forgiven thee.”

02:35.352 --> 02:41.324 align:center line:79%
“Damsel, I say unto thee,
arise, be thou clean.”

02:41.892 --> 02:43.760 align:center line:81%
“Neither do I condemn thee:

02:43.960 --> 02:49.366 align:center line:79%
Go, and sin no more.”
“Daughter, be of good comfort:

02:49.366 --> 02:51.368 align:center line:81%
Thy faith hath made thee whole;

02:51.568 --> 02:52.803 align:center line:81%
Go in peace.”

02:54.204 --> 02:57.507 align:center line:79%
The Savior's words
to these individuals were brief,

02:57.841 --> 03:03.647 align:center line:79%
but with them He painted vast new horizons
of forgiveness, healing,

03:03.980 --> 03:07.751 align:center line:81%
restoration, peace, and eternal life.

03:08.385 --> 03:14.224 align:center line:79%
And the glorious news is, He offers
the same new beginning to you and to me.

03:15.325 --> 03:20.130 align:center line:79%
All of us can have a new beginning
through and because of Jesus Christ.

03:20.430 --> 03:26.369 align:center line:79%
Even you. New beginnings are at the heart
of the Father’s plan for His children.

03:26.703 --> 03:30.440 align:center line:81%
This is the church of new beginnings.

03:31.174 --> 03:33.176 align:center line:81%
This is the church of fresh starts.

03:35.345 --> 03:37.481 align:center line:81%
With baptism by water and the Spirit,

03:37.481 --> 03:41.051 align:center line:79%
we are born again and can walk
in newness of life.

03:42.285 --> 03:45.655 align:center line:79%
How much hope does that new
beginning bring to one

03:45.655 --> 03:47.891 align:center line:81%
who has trudged under the burden of sin,

03:48.191 --> 03:50.694 align:center line:79%
or suffered from the effects
of a troubled life

03:50.694 --> 03:52.462 align:center line:81%
and dysfunctional relationships?

03:53.430 --> 03:58.468 align:center line:79%
Jesus needed no forgiveness of sin
Himself or a fresh start in life,

03:58.502 --> 04:03.273 align:center line:79%
yet He was baptized,
showing us in high relief the way

04:03.774 --> 04:07.611 align:center line:79%
to the new beginning
He has carved for each of us.

04:09.179 --> 04:12.282 align:center line:79%
And our new beginning
doesn't just happen once.

04:12.616 --> 04:16.853 align:center line:79%
We tend to think that baptism is our one
shot at a new beginning.

04:17.521 --> 04:21.258 align:center line:81%
It isn't. We don't have just one chance.

04:21.825 --> 04:24.261 align:center line:81%
These new beginnings can happen every day,

04:25.362 --> 04:27.531 align:center line:81%
and certainly every week

04:27.597 --> 04:29.199 align:center line:81%
as we eat a small piece of bread

04:29.199 --> 04:32.235 align:center line:79%
and drink a tiny cup
of water in remembrance

04:32.235 --> 04:34.671 align:center line:81%
of the gift of our perfect Savior,

04:35.372 --> 04:40.377 align:center line:79%
who died for the express
purpose of giving us

04:40.377 --> 04:42.746 align:center line:81%
as many new beginnings as we need.

04:45.448 --> 04:50.320 align:center line:79%
Jesus gives us as many new
beginnings as we need.

04:51.888 --> 04:55.091 align:center line:79%
With commitment and rejoicing
in a new life in Christ,

04:55.125 --> 04:58.995 align:center line:79%
we can become a new
creature where old things pass away

04:58.995 --> 05:00.831 align:center line:81%
and all things become new.

05:01.531 --> 05:06.069 align:center line:79%
What reprieve does that kind
of new dawn bring to a soul

05:06.069 --> 05:10.740 align:center line:79%
who keeps trying through continuing
to choose faith in our Redeemer's power

05:10.740 --> 05:16.880 align:center line:79%
to heal and restore, despite the crushing
setbacks of living in a fallen world?

05:18.215 --> 05:23.320 align:center line:79%
The Savior never gave up on His commitment
to fulfill the will of the Father

05:23.320 --> 05:26.523 align:center line:81%
and complete His divine atoning mission,

05:26.857 --> 05:31.394 align:center line:79%
even through the pain that caused Him
to tremble, to bleed from every pore,

05:31.595 --> 05:38.568 align:center line:79%
to suffer body and spirit, and pray that
the bitter cup might be removed. Again,

05:38.835 --> 05:43.506 align:center line:79%
He was demonstrating for us what
faithful endurance with God looks like.

05:45.108 --> 05:49.379 align:center line:79%
With every covenant we make
and every effort we give to keep it,

05:49.412 --> 05:54.317 align:center line:79%
we can receive a new heart and a fuller
measure of a new spirit.

05:54.818 --> 05:59.122 align:center line:79%
Little by little, the more we invite
His goodness into our hearts

05:59.422 --> 06:04.227 align:center line:79%
and cast out the self-defeating
voices in our heads,

06:04.628 --> 06:08.465 align:center line:79%
we become His people
because we truly make Him our God.

06:09.332 --> 06:15.472 align:center line:79%
Jesus so keenly wants to be our King
and our Shepherd and our Prince of Peace,

06:16.239 --> 06:21.311 align:center line:79%
and we can choose to make Him so
in our own hearts and minds.

06:23.546 --> 06:26.950 align:center line:79%
Repentance opens the door
to our new beginnings,

06:26.950 --> 06:29.185 align:center line:81%
fresh starts, and second chances.

06:29.452 --> 06:32.322 align:center line:79%
Our dear President Nelson's
teachings have cleared up

06:32.322 --> 06:35.425 align:center line:79%
misconceptions about
the divine gift of repentance,

06:35.692 --> 06:39.663 align:center line:81%
and I think we finally begin to grasp it.

06:40.563 --> 06:44.701 align:center line:79%
It's exciting to hear our youth
describe what repentance means to them.

06:44.701 --> 06:48.538 align:center line:79%
I recently heard a young woman say,
with a smile on her face,

06:48.538 --> 06:52.976 align:center line:79%
and I quote, “When I think
of repentance—daily repentance—

06:52.976 --> 06:55.178 align:center line:81%
I feel incredible joy and hope.

06:55.712 --> 06:59.249 align:center line:79%
I feel the love and happiness
of my Heavenly Father and my Savior.

07:00.050 --> 07:02.886 align:center line:79%
I'm not afraid to come
to Heavenly Father in prayer

07:02.886 --> 07:06.089 align:center line:79%
and ask for His help
with whatever I’m struggling with.

07:06.756 --> 07:10.293 align:center line:79%
I know They’re not trying to catch
me doing something wrong.

07:11.094 --> 07:13.964 align:center line:81%
Their arms are open wide.

07:14.698 --> 07:18.168 align:center line:81%
This is repentance to me,” she said.

07:20.170 --> 07:23.573 align:center line:79%
This young woman understands
that because of Jesus Christ,

07:23.940 --> 07:26.810 align:center line:81%
she can have new beginnings.

07:27.911 --> 07:29.713 align:center line:81%
Do you need a new beginning?

07:30.680 --> 07:32.282 align:center line:81%
Can you make a fresh start?

07:32.482 --> 07:33.483 align:center line:81%
Even you?

07:35.018 --> 07:38.955 align:center line:79%
Think about the people the Savior
ministered to—the people

07:38.955 --> 07:41.825 align:center line:79%
He taught, healed, raised,
forgave, and restored.

07:42.425 --> 07:46.296 align:center line:79%
Was He selecting them from a particular
economic class or background?

07:46.396 --> 07:49.632 align:center line:79%
Was He distinguishing between
the righteous and the sinful?

07:49.632 --> 07:54.871 align:center line:79%
Was He singling people out because they
were more deserving or more loved? No.

07:56.172 --> 07:58.074 align:center line:81%
Some came to Him with great faith,

07:58.074 --> 08:02.679 align:center line:79%
believing in His power to heal, like
the woman with the issue of blood,

08:02.812 --> 08:05.582 align:center line:79%
the Roman centurion
whose servant was dying,

08:05.815 --> 08:09.753 align:center line:81%
the leper, Jairus, and blind Bartimaeus.

08:10.053 --> 08:12.322 align:center line:81%
They each put their faith on the line,

08:12.322 --> 08:13.690 align:center line:81%
hoping that the goodness

08:13.690 --> 08:17.360 align:center line:79%
and power of the Rabbi
from Nazareth would change

08:17.360 --> 08:19.329 align:center line:81%
their lives and their prospects.

08:19.796 --> 08:23.199 align:center line:81%
And He did. He let His healing flow.

08:24.267 --> 08:28.505 align:center line:79%
But Jesus also blessed
those who had wavering faith,

08:28.872 --> 08:32.909 align:center line:79%
like the father of the sick child
who cried out, perhaps as you have,

08:33.376 --> 08:36.880 align:center line:79%
“Lord, I believe;
help thou mine unbelief.”

08:37.680 --> 08:41.618 align:center line:79%
And He even poured out compassion
upon those who hadn’t sought Him at all,

08:42.018 --> 08:45.255 align:center line:79%
like the woman taken in adultery,
the widow of Nain,

08:45.288 --> 08:49.759 align:center line:79%
the disabled man at the pool of Bethesda,
and the man born blind.

08:50.994 --> 08:55.365 align:center line:79%
Have you felt Him going
about doing good in your life,

08:55.632 --> 08:58.735 align:center line:79%
even when you haven’t been seeking
Him or following Him?

08:59.436 --> 09:04.074 align:center line:79%
To each of these scriptural figures
and to all who would listen and respond,

09:04.374 --> 09:07.377 align:center line:81%
He gave a new beginning,

09:07.977 --> 09:13.416 align:center line:79%
whether it was a new life forgiven
of sin, or a new life healed of disease,

09:13.616 --> 09:16.252 align:center line:81%
or a new life raised from death.

09:17.087 --> 09:19.923 align:center line:81%
What does this mean for you and for me?

09:21.091 --> 09:25.662 align:center line:79%
His goodness and mercy and loving
kindness know no bounds.

09:26.329 --> 09:30.900 align:center line:79%
New beginnings are at the heart
of the Father’s plan.

09:31.434 --> 09:36.072 align:center line:79%
Fresh starts are the mission
of the Son.

09:37.173 --> 09:38.842 align:center line:81%
New dawns, new chapters,

09:38.842 --> 09:45.014 align:center line:79%
and new chances are the simple
core of the gospel's good news.

09:46.116 --> 09:52.122 align:center line:79%
So have you been away too long from
your covenants to receive a new beginning?

09:52.655 --> 09:53.656 align:center line:81%
No.

09:54.257 --> 09:59.028 align:center line:79%
Have you done this or that too
many times to be given another chance?

09:59.462 --> 10:02.699 align:center line:79%
No. Have you gone too
far from Christ for Him

10:02.699 --> 10:05.602 align:center line:79%
to help you write a new
story from here on out?

10:06.269 --> 10:07.270 align:center line:81%
No.

10:08.104 --> 10:12.675 align:center line:79%
The adversary is the only one who benefits
from the idea that you’re sunk.

10:14.010 --> 10:15.145 align:center line:81%
You are not.

10:17.480 --> 10:21.151 align:center line:79%
And new beginnings are for more
than just our sins and mistakes.

10:21.317 --> 10:23.653 align:center line:79%
Through the goodness
and grace of the Savior,

10:23.653 --> 10:28.391 align:center line:79%
we can have fresh starts
that propel change in old mindsets,

10:28.558 --> 10:30.994 align:center line:81%
bad habits, grumpy dispositions,

10:31.961 --> 10:35.298 align:center line:79%
negative attitudes,
feelings of powerlessness,

10:35.298 --> 10:37.700 align:center line:81%
and tendencies to blame others

10:37.700 --> 10:40.203 align:center line:81%
and avoid personal responsibility.

10:40.870 --> 10:46.075 align:center line:79%
You can actually change things about
yourself that have been wearing you down

10:46.075 --> 10:50.880 align:center line:79%
for years. You can start
again through the might

10:51.080 --> 10:53.716 align:center line:81%
of the Master of new beginnings.

10:54.317 --> 10:59.422 align:center line:79%
He never tires of giving
those new beginnings to us.

11:00.490 --> 11:04.494 align:center line:79%
To those who are struggling
with the same sin or the same setback over

11:04.494 --> 11:06.763 align:center line:81%
and over again, you keep going.

11:07.030 --> 11:11.801 align:center line:79%
He’s hasn’t put
a roadblock in front of you.

11:11.834 --> 11:14.804 align:center line:79%
He hasn't set a limit
on your second chances.

11:15.038 --> 11:17.674 align:center line:81%
You press on. You keep striving.

11:17.807 --> 11:20.009 align:center line:81%
You seek help from those around you.

11:20.243 --> 11:24.214 align:center line:79%
And you trust in the new
beginning that is there for you

11:24.247 --> 11:28.651 align:center line:79%
every time you turn back
to your Father in sincerity of heart.

11:29.219 --> 11:30.720 align:center line:81%
Leave deliberate sinning,

11:31.421 --> 11:36.025 align:center line:79%
casual repeats, and prideful
rebellion behind you where they belong.

11:36.893 --> 11:39.963 align:center line:79%
You don't have to be who
you've been before.

11:41.631 --> 11:46.502 align:center line:79%
Embrace your fresh start,
your second or third or fourth

11:46.502 --> 11:52.175 align:center line:79%
or hundredth chance offered to you
through the atoning blood of Jesus Christ.

11:52.976 --> 11:57.247 align:center line:79%
I am grateful beyond description
for the new beginnings I've been given,

11:57.580 --> 12:00.617 align:center line:81%
and for those I will yet be offered.

12:02.018 --> 12:05.488 align:center line:79%
Our Savior uttered one
final understatement,

12:05.655 --> 12:10.159 align:center line:79%
without which there would be no cause
for hope or rejoicing this day.

12:11.828 --> 12:17.800 align:center line:79%
After the agonies of Gethsemane and at
the conclusion of the torturous cross,

12:18.301 --> 12:23.306 align:center line:81%
He simply said, “It is finished.”

12:25.408 --> 12:27.710 align:center line:81%
Messianic prophecy had been fulfilled

12:27.710 --> 12:31.514 align:center line:79%
and the full payment
of the debt for humanity's sins

12:31.848 --> 12:33.783 align:center line:81%
and suffering had been paid.

12:34.150 --> 12:40.890 align:center line:79%
He declared finished His infinite
and eternal sacrifice;

12:41.791 --> 12:47.196 align:center line:79%
yet His Atonement would not
be complete until He Himself

12:47.196 --> 12:50.700 align:center line:81%
experienced new life on the third day,

12:51.634 --> 12:56.172 align:center line:81%
the new beginning as a glorified,

12:56.306 --> 13:00.510 align:center line:79%
resurrected being through
the power of the Father.

13:02.945 --> 13:06.149 align:center line:79%
Because He always did those things
which pleased His Father,

13:06.149 --> 13:09.285 align:center line:79%
and because He suffered
the will of the Father in all things,

13:09.285 --> 13:11.754 align:center line:81%
you and I can have new beginnings.

13:12.889 --> 13:18.594 align:center line:79%
Please receive your new
beginning even today,

13:19.862 --> 13:20.863 align:center line:81%
right now.

13:22.165 --> 13:25.702 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ is the Author
and Finisher of our faith,

13:25.702 --> 13:28.504 align:center line:81%
writing countless new chapters with us.

13:28.771 --> 13:30.940 align:center line:81%
He is the Beginning and the End—

13:31.240 --> 13:37.980 align:center line:79%
the end of our shame and suffering
and the beginning of a new life in Him,

13:38.147 --> 13:39.549 align:center line:81%
letting us receive

13:41.551 --> 13:49.459 align:center line:79%
His grace and leave the past
behind and begin again with a new dawn,

13:49.692 --> 13:52.095 align:center line:81%
as many times as we need.

13:52.495 --> 13:59.902 align:center line:79%
Truly His “goodness and mercy shall
follow [us] all the days of our lives.”

14:00.403 --> 14:03.639 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

